            <ArticleTitle>Pyogenic sacro-iliitis, a rare cause of peripartum pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient was presented suffering from severe pelvic pain several weeks after delivery. Symptoms pointed in the direction of a peripartum pelvic pain syndrome. One week after admission, the clinical course deteriorated. An infective endocarditis complicated by pyogenic sacro-iliitis was diagnosed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
